course: dictionary
lesson: 2496
title: Many meanings of dearly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word dearly is a good example. The first meaning is very much. «I love you dearly» means I love you very much. Try swapping in very much: the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: The second meaning is at a high cost, with suffering or loss. «Coal powered the Industrial Revolution, but miners paid dearly: explosions, roof falls and lung disease.» The list after the colon is the clue. Those dangers show that paid dearly means they suffered a heavy price.
explain: The third meaning is formal. «Dearly beloved» is used at the start of a church wedding or funeral to greet the people there. «The dearly departed» means someone who has died. It is a polite way to say it, and people sometimes use it jokingly.
fact: Dearly is an adverb, a word that tells you more about a verb, such as how much someone loves.
fact: «Dearly» means very much, as in «love dearly» or «would dearly like a puppy».
fact: «Dearly» can mean at a high cost, as in «paid dearly» for a mistake.
fact: «Dearly beloved» is a formal greeting at a church wedding or funeral.
fact: To choose the meaning, look at the clues: deep feeling means very much, and a heavy price or loss means at a high cost.
exercise: «I love you dearly.» What does dearly mean here? | Quickly | Sadly | At a high cost | *Very much
exercise: «Miners paid dearly for coal, with explosions and roof falls.» What does paid dearly mean? | Paid a small amount of money | *Suffered a heavy price | Paid early | Paid with a cheque
exercise: «The dearly departed» is a polite way to talk about whom? | A teacher on holiday | *A person who has died | A friend who has moved house | A dog that ran away
test: «She would dearly like a puppy.» Which meaning fits? | Not at all | At a low cost | *Very much | Quite fast
test: Which phrase is a formal greeting used at the start of a church wedding? | Dear diary | Dear me | Dearly paid | *Dearly beloved
exam: «The children paid dearly for their mistake.» Which meaning fits best? | Very much | Happily | Quietly | *At a high cost
